  "live_records": {
    "q-158571": {
      "dom_id": "step-q158571",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Evaluate $z=\\frac{2y-x}{{x}^{3}-{y}^{2}-4}$ at the point $(2,-2).$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(2,-2),$ we substitute $x=2$ and $y=-2$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\,{|}_{(2,-2)} & =\\frac{2y-x}{{x}^{3}-{y}^{2}-4}\\,{|}_{(2,-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(-2)-2}{{2}^{3}-(-2)^{2}-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4-2}{8-4-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-6)}{0},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined.",
