      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Evaluate $z={x}^{2}+xy-5$ at the point $(1,2).$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(1,2),$ we substitute $x=1$ and $y=2$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\,{|}_{(1,2)} & =({x}^{2}+xy-5)\\,{|}_{(1,2)} \\\\  & =(1)^{2}+(1)(2)-5 \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
