    "q-158572": {
      "dom_id": "step-q158572",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Evaluate $z=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x-2y+4)$ at the point $(-4,1).$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(-4,1),$ we substitute $x=-4$ and $y=1$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\,{|}_{(-4,1)} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x-2y+4)\\,{|}_{(-4,1)} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3(-4)-2(1)+4) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-12-2+4) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-10),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined.",
