    "q-158554": {
      "dom_id": "step-q158554",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\ne 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\ne 0\\}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
