    "q-158185": {
      "dom_id": "step-q158185",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-y)}{{e}^{x}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the logarithm is positive, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nNotice that ${e}^{x}>0$ for all $x.$ Therefore, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y>0\\,⟹\\,x>y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x>y\\}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-158185-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ne y\\}",
